    "q-237511": {
      "dom_id": "step-q237511",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/530a07a528037b95227f1616d9a74e56874a839e2396a1cb053a417e4407659d.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate the value of $4÷\\frac{5}{6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate $4÷\\frac{5}{6}$, we first need to divide each of the $4$ wholes into $6$ equal parts.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/90771544aed1e49a45f857d5fe041476a0f8e6130c87466f6853e76468f1fa14.png)\n\n \n\nNext, we break this into groups of $5$:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/2343c93c7c92c4510b5f19b2cd3d9e2221da6f69996009ac4e6b669bbcac5278.png)\n\n \n\nNote the following: \n\n- We got $\\boxed{\\text{4}}$ full groups.\n\n- There are $4$ pieces left over out of a possible group of $5.$ So the fractional part of our answer is \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n4÷\\frac{5}{6}=\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\,\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
