    "q-237502": {
      "dom_id": "step-q237502",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/38a8f6963fbe538fc67310e583271d8feeef3b86ec9f1e81354f179fe727963f.png)\n\nIf the model above represents $1$ whole, use the model to solve the following division problem. Express your answer as a mixed number in its simplest form.\n\n$1÷\\frac{3}{8}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate $1÷\\frac{3}{8}$, we first need to divide the whole into $8$ equal parts.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/e5c3ad39f7ebf8bb6585dfa65054bb6b0eba881f1e9f7404ae5275f5c45f3771.png)\n\n \n\nNext, we break this into groups of $3$:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/dbfd34916dd6db9467988b6b72052f9b077e4de67e2b54b9a092d959233ccc85.png)\n\n \n\nNote the following: \n\n- We got $\\boxed{\\text{2}}$ full groups.\n\n- There are $2$ parts left over out of a possible group of $3.$ So the fractional part of our answer is \n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n1÷\\frac{3}{8}=\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\,\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
